Ladybird now resumes a waiting resource selection from a media element
task, queues that resumption again on adoption, and drops the selector
when a new load begins. Run in Chrome 157.0.8103.79, Firefox 151.0, and
WebKit 26.5, none of the three engines crashes when a source is
appended to, or moved into, a waiting video in a removed iframe’s
document. Once such a video is adopted into a fully active document,
Firefox and WebKit load the source (or the src set before adoption), as
Ladybird now does; Chrome loads neither.
